---

<Layout
  title="BIP-110 Code Walkthrough"
  description="A public guide to the Bitcoin Knots BIP-110 code: what changes, why it matters, where to verify it, and how the temporary deployment works."
  ogImage="/images/bip110-og-code-walkthrough-dark.png"
>
  <main class="min-h-screen">
    <Header />

    <section class="px-6 pt-24 pb-14">
      <div
        class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_22rem] lg:items-end"
      >
        <div>
          <p
            class="mb-4 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary"
          >
            Public guide to the code
          </p>
          <h1 class="max-w-4xl text-4xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-5xl">
            BIP-110 Code Walkthrough
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
            Follow BIP-110 in Bitcoin Knots with the important checks
            highlighted and explained in plain language. Begin with the code
            review, then use the rule reference below to connect each check to
            the seven consensus limits and the temporary activation,
            grandfathering, and expiry logic.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
            <a
              href="#code-review"
              class="inline-flex h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-5 text-sm font-semibold text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/40"
            >
              Review code notes
            </a>
            <a
              href="#rule-reference"
              class="inline-flex h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-border/70 bg-background px-5 text-sm font-semibold transition-colors hover:border-primary/40 hover:text-primary focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/40"
            >
              Rule reference
            </a>
            <a
              href={sourceUrl}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="inline-flex h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-border/70 bg-background px-5 text-sm font-semibold transition-colors hover:border-primary/40 hover:text-primary focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/40"
            >
              Original Bitcoin Knots review
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside
          aria-label="Source review summary"
          class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border/60 bg-card/60"
        >
          <div class="border-b border-border/60 p-5">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">Source overview</p>
              <span
                class="rounded-full border border-primary/30 bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-primary"
              >
                BIP-110
              </span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
              Use the linked source files to verify each check in the tagged
              Bitcoin Knots release, then cross-check it against the rule
              reference below.
            </p>
          </div>

          <dl class="grid grid-cols-2 border-b border-border/60">
            {
              heroFacts.map(([value, label]) => (
                <div class="border-r border-b border-border/60 p-4 even:border-r-0 [&:nth-last-child(-n+2)]:border-b-0">
                  <dt class="text-xs leading-5 text-muted-foreground">
                    {label}
                  </dt>
                  <dd class="mt-1 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">
                    {value}
                  </dd>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </dl>

          <div class="bg-muted/35 p-5">
            <a
              href={githubBaseUrl}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="group block text-xs font-medium text-muted-foreground transition-colors hover:text-primary focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/40"
            >
              GitHub tag
              <span
                class="mt-1 block break-all font-mono text-[11px] text-foreground/80 group-hover:text-primary"
              >
                {githubTag}
              </span>
            </a>
            <a
              href="#code-review"
              class="mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-primary/30 bg-background px-4 text-sm font-semibold text-primary transition-colors hover:bg-primary hover:text-primary-foreground focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/40"
            >
              Start with the code
            </a>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="code-review" class="scroll-mt-24 px-6 py-14">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
        <div class="mb-8 border-y border-border/60 py-8">
          <div>
            <p
              class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary"
            >
              Guided source
            </p>
            <div
              class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_22rem] lg:items-end"
            >
              <div>
                <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">
                  Code with plain-language notes
                </h2>
                <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-muted-foreground">
                  Each panel shows the important C++ lines, why they matter, and
                  a direct link to the tagged source. Notes stay attached to the
                  lines they explain, so the source remains the main reading
                  surface.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 lg:justify-end">
                <span
                  class="inline-flex h-8 items-center rounded-full border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 px-3 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-700 dark:border-emerald-900/70 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 dark:text-emerald-300"
                >
                  + new check
                </span>
                <span
                  class="inline-flex h-8 items-center rounded-full border border-red-200 bg-red-50 px-3 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 dark:border-red-900/70 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-300"
                >
                  - replaced path
                </span>
                <a
                  href={githubBaseUrl}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  class="inline-flex h-8 max-w-full items-center rounded-full border border-border/70 bg-background px-3 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground transition-colors hover:border-primary/40 hover:text-primary focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/40"
                >
                  <span class="mr-1 text-foreground/70">tag</span>
                  <span class="truncate">{githubTag}</span>
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-10">
          {
            codeSections.map((section) => (
              <article
                id={section.id}
                class="scroll-mt-24 rounded-xl border border-border/70 bg-card/60"
              >
                <div class="grid gap-5 border-b border-border/60 p-5 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_18rem]">
                  <div>
                    <a
                      href={githubFileUrl(section.file)}
                      target="_blank"
                      rel="noopener noreferrer"
                      class="font-mono text-sm text-primary break-all underline-offset-4 hover:underline focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/40"
                    >
                      {section.file}
                    </a>
                    <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold">{section.title}</h3>
                    <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
                      {section.summary}
                    </p>
                    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
                      <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground">
                        Related
                      </span>
                      {section.references.map((reference) => (
                        <a
                          href={reference.href}
                          class={referenceChipClass}
                          aria-label={`Jump to ${reference.label} reference`}
                        >
                          {reference.label}
                        </a>
                      ))}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 lg:items-end">
                    <a
                      href={section.href}
                      target="_blank"
                      rel="noopener noreferrer"
                      class="inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-border/70 bg-background px-4 text-sm font-semibold transition-colors hover:border-primary/40 hover:text-primary focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/40"
                    >
                      GitHub lines
                    </a>
                    <a
                      href={sourceUrl}
                      target="_blank"
                      rel="noopener noreferrer"
                      class="text-sm text-muted-foreground underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary hover:underline focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/40"
                    >
                      Original walkthrough
                    </a>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <div
                    class="code-scroll overflow-x-auto bg-muted/40 py-4"
                    aria-label={`${section.title} source code`}
                  >
                    <div class="min-w-full">
                      {section.lines.map((line) => {
                        const note = section.notes.find(
                          (item) => item.line === line.number,
                        );

                        return (
                          <div class={codeLineClass(line.type)}>
                            <span class={codeLineMarkerClass(line.type)}>
                              {codeLineMarker(line.type)}
                            </span>
                            <span class="select-none text-right text-muted-foreground/70">
                              {line.number}
                            </span>
                            <div class="flex min-w-max items-start gap-3">
                              <span class="whitespace-pre">
                                {highlightCpp(line.code).map((token) => (
                                  <span
                                    class="syntax-token"
                                    style={token.style}
                                  >
                                    {token.text}
                                  </span>
                                ))}
                              </span>
                              {note && (
                                <details
                                  class="line-note"
                                  name="code-walkthrough-line-note"
                                >
                                  <summary
                                    id={`${section.id}-note-${note.line}`}
                                    style={`anchor-name: --${section.id}-note-${note.line}`}
                                    aria-label={`Show note for line ${note.line}`}
                                    class="line-note-trigger"
                                  >
                                    note
                                  </summary>
                                  <div
                                    class="line-note-card"
                                    style={`position-anchor: --${section.id}-note-${note.line}`}
                                  >
                                    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold text-primary">
                                      line {note.line}
                                    </p>
                                    <p class="mt-1 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">
                                      {note.title}
                                    </p>
                                    <p class="mt-2 font-sans text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
                                      {note.text}
                                    </p>
                                  </div>
                                </details>
                              )}
                            </div>
                          </div>
                        );
                      })}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="rule-reference" class="scroll-mt-24 px-6 py-14">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
        <div class="mb-8 max-w-3xl">
          <p
            class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary"
          >
            Rule reference
          </p>
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">Seven rules, one enforcement flag</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
            The easiest way to understand BIP-110 is rule by rule. Rule 1 limits
            new transaction outputs. Rules 2 through 7 apply while scripts are
            being checked, once the reduced-data flag is active.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid gap-3">
          {
            rules.map((rule) => (
              <article
                id={rule.id}
                class="scroll-mt-24 grid gap-4 rounded-xl border border-border/60 bg-card/50 p-5 md:grid-cols-[8rem_minmax(0,1fr)_16rem] md:items-start"
              >
                <div class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-primary">
                  {rule.label}
                </div>
                <div>
                  <h3 class="font-semibold">{rule.title}</h3>
                  <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
                    {rule.text}
                  </p>
                </div>
                <a
                  href={githubFileUrl(rule.code)}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  class="rounded-lg bg-muted/60 px-3 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground transition-colors hover:text-primary focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/40 md:text-right"
                >
                  {rule.code}
                </a>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 border-t border-border/60 pt-6">
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold text-muted-foreground">
            Deployment references
          </p>
          <div class="grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-2">
            {
              topicReferences.map((reference) => (
                <article
                  id={reference.id}
                  class="scroll-mt-24 rounded-xl border border-border/60 bg-card/40 p-4"
                >
                  <div class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-primary">
                    {reference.label}
                  </div>
                  <h3 class="mt-2 font-semibold">{reference.title}</h3>
                  <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
                    {reference.text}
                  </p>
                </article>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="px-6 py-14">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
        <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[20rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
          <div>
            <p
              class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary"
            >
              Reading order
            </p>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">Follow the change in five steps</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
              This order keeps the review simple: output limits, activation,
              script checks, grandfathering, then expiry.
            </p>
          </div>

          <ol class="grid gap-4">
            {
              readingPasses.map((pass, index) => (
                <li class="grid gap-4 rounded-xl border border-border/60 bg-card/50 p-5 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
                  <span class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-primary">
                    {String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}
                  </span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold">{pass.name}</h3>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
                      {pass.detail}
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="verification-map" class="scroll-mt-24 px-6 py-14">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
        <div class="mb-8 max-w-3xl">
          <p
            class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary"
          >
            Verification map
          </p>
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">Where to verify each part</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
            Use this as a checklist while reading the source. Each file has a
            narrow job, so the change is easier to verify piece by piece.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-5">
          {
            files.map((item) => (
              <article class="rounded-xl border border-border/60 bg-card/50 p-5">
                <div class="grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_16rem]">
                  <div>
                    <a
                      href={githubFileUrl(item.file)}
                      target="_blank"
                      rel="noopener noreferrer"
                      class="font-mono text-sm text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/40"
                    >
                      {item.file}
                    </a>
                    <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold">{item.label}</h3>
                    <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
                      {item.summary}
                    </p>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-foreground">
                      Covers
                    </p>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                      {item.rules.map((rule) => (
                        <span class="rounded-full border border-border/70 bg-background px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium">
                          {rule}
                        </span>
                      ))}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-3">
                  {item.details.map((detail) => (
                    <li class="rounded-lg bg-muted/50 p-4 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
                      {detail}
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="px-6 py-14">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
        <div
          class="rounded-xl border border-primary/30 bg-primary/5 p-6 md:p-8"
        >
          <div
            class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_18rem] lg:items-center"
          >
            <div>
              <p
                class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary"
              >
                Important nuance
              </p>
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Grandfathering is per input</h2>
              <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
                BIP-110 does not treat a transaction as all old rules or all new
                rules. During block connection, each input is compared with the
                activation height. Inputs spending coins created before
                activation clear the reduced-data flags, while other inputs in
                the same transaction can still be checked under the new rules.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div
              class="rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-background/70 p-4"
            >
              <p class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-primary">
                flags_per_input
              </p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
                This is why script-check caching is bypassed when per-input
                overrides exist. The cache key assumes one flag set for every
                input.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="px-6 pt-14 pb-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl border-t border-border/60 pt-10">
        <div
          class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_18rem] md:items-start"
        >
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Read the original code review</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
              This page is a structured guide to the Bitcoin Knots walkthrough.
              The original contains the C++ snippets beside line-by-line
              explanations, so it is the best place to compare this guide
              against the source.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a
            href={sourceUrl}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-5 text-sm font-semibold text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/40"
          >
            Open original review
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Footer />
  </main>
</Layout>

